@startuml flow-config-load
!theme plain
title Flow config load: resolve closure -> narrow check against kernel-policy/1 -> confirmation -> atomic activation with migrations -> generation fence

actor "Process designer\n(agent or person)" as Dev
database "Project repo\n(default branch)" as Git
participant "B2 Flow engine\n(config loader)" as FE
participant "Environment\n(curator playbook check)" as Env
participant "Kernel guards\n(kernel-policy/1)" as KG
participant "Trust\n(confirmed / granted / narrowed)" as T
actor "Confirmer\n(person)" as P
database "B1 Task store" as TS
participant "Running worker\n(pinned to D7, g12)" as W

Dev -> Git: commit Playbook.json (adds design-task,\npins analysis -> solution-architect)
FE -> Git: read Playbook.json at default-branch head\n(never the working tree)
FE -> Env: resolve extends/uses pinned by digest;\nportable + machine checks
Env --> FE: resolved closure, digest D8, report
alt check fails
  FE -> TS: append notice "proposed head invalid"; keep D7 in force
else valid
  FE -> KG: narrow_check(resolved closure + migrations)
  KG -> KG: every state has a kernel class; no path skips\nK1 CR acceptance, K3 landing, K5 review evidence;\nno limit above ceilings (K4); no goal writes (K6); audit kept (K7)
  alt widens a kernel predicate
    KG --> FE: rejected widen:K<n>:<rule>
    FE -> TS: notice "activation refused: widens K<n>"; keep D7
    note right of KG
      A person's confirmation cannot waive this.
      kernel-policy/1 changes only with a kernel
      release installed by the operator (R55).
    end note
  else narrowing only
    KG --> FE: ok
    FE -> TS: list elements in states that D8 removes or reclassifies
    alt stranded elements and no migrations declared
      FE -> TS: notice "activation refused: stranded elements"; keep D7
    else none stranded, or migrations declared
      FE -> FE: diff D7 -> D8 by section
      FE -> T: granted(process, kind) for each difference
      alt every difference covered by a capability
        T --> FE: covered
      else workflow structure or authority changed (role pins, transitions)
        T --> FE: not covered
        FE -> TS: pending D8; notify confirmers
        note right of FE
          Until confirmed, the whole D7
          runs; later commits wait too
        end note
        P -> T: task-board trust confirm (head D8)
        T --> FE: confirmed(D8)
      end
      FE -> TS: activate D8 in one transaction:\nactivation lock (transitions wait), migrations\n(actor=kernel, through kguard), version in force D8,\ngeneration g12 -> g13, release
    end
  end
end

== In-flight tasks after activation ==
note over TS, W
  Each status record and board_ref carries flow_digest and flow_generation.
  A running worker keeps its launch pin (profile_pin) until it hands off.
end note
W -> FE: transition(TASK-42, development -> testing)\nboard_ref D7, g12
FE -> FE: evaluate under D8 (the version in force now, g13)
alt D8 still admits the run's role in its state
  FE -> TS: write_status(proposal, expected rev, g13)
  TS -> TS: kguard K1-K8; commit (flow_digest D8)
else state removed or owner changed
  FE --> W: refused (stale run)
  FE -> TS: element owned by the root orchestrator (PB 6.1)
end
@enduml
